  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mo>+</mo><mtext>ve</mtext></mrow> </math> polarity is connected to <math> <mtext>A</mtext> </math><br /><br />Then <math><msub><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is forward biased and <math><msub><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is reversed biased i.e.<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e407a9e1-6f04-4610-bd03-711e216d304f-image.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 136px;\" /><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> current through <math><msub><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>A</mn></math><br /><br />When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mo>+</mo><mtext>ve</mtext></mrow> </math> polarity is connected to <math> <mtext>B</mtext> </math> then <math><msub><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is forward biased and <math><msub><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is reversed biased then<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6f2e266c-7796-45ea-99bc-3d1bc7b16a2b-image.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 131px;\" /><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2&#160; </mn><mn>A</mn></math>",
